@*
    OdsAvatar — a circular identity token (Odyssey Design System · components/Avatar).

    Image (Src), text monogram (Initials or child content), or a Material glyph
    (Icon), in that precedence. A MudAvatar with the Odyssey size steps
    (sm = 28 · md = 40 · lg = 56) and tone (neutral default / tide brand-tinted).

    THE IMAGE IS A PLAIN <img>, not MudImage. MudImage exposes none of `loading`,
    `decoding` or `onerror` naturally, and this was the client's ONLY MudImage
    call site — OdsPhotoTile and JournalPhotoGallery already use a bare <img> for
    exactly these attributes. `loading="lazy"` + `decoding="async"` are not an
    optimisation here but a requirement: a contact list under no-cache issues one
    conditional GET per avatar, so the off-screen ones must defer.

    `Fit` decides how an image meets the frame. Cover (default) square-crops — a
    person's photograph. Contain LETTERBOXES it on a neutral ground with a 3:1
    boundary — a company logo, which carries transparency, is rarely square and
    must never be cut. Choose it from what the image IS, not from the shape: a
    wordmark cropped to a circle is unrecognisable.

    `OnError` fires when the image cannot load (deleted file, revoked access,
    offline). The CONSUMER uses it to swap back to its identity glyph, silently —
    the failure is never surfaced to the user. Without it a broken image renders
    the browser's broken-image icon inside the frame.
*@

@* A non-image avatar is a meaningful `img` only when it carries an accessible
   name (Alt). Unlabeled icon/monogram avatars are decorative reinforcement —
   the entity name already sits in the adjacent cell — so they're aria-hidden
   rather than an unlabeled `role="img"` (Odyssey Design System · a11y pass:
   decorative avatars carry no img role). *@
<MudAvatar Style="@AvatarStyle"
           Color="@(Tone == OdsAvatarTone.Tide ? Color.Primary : Color.Default)"
           Variant="Variant.Filled"
           role="@AvatarRole"
           aria-label="@(string.IsNullOrEmpty(Alt) ? null : Alt)"
           aria-hidden="@(IsDecorative ? "true" : null)"
           Class="@RootClass"
           @attributes="UserAttributes">
    @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Src))
    {
        @* alt="" plus the parent's aria-hidden when the adjacent cell already
           names the subject; a descriptive Alt where the image is the subject of
           its own controls. Both are the caller's call, never guessed here. *@
        <img src="@Src" alt="@Alt" loading="lazy" decoding="async" @onerror="OnErrorAsync" />
    }
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Icon))
    {
        <MudIcon Icon="@Icon" />
    }
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(Initials))
    {
        @Initials
    }
    else
    {
        @ChildContent
    }
</MudAvatar>

@code {
    /// <summary>Image source. Takes precedence over initials / icon.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Src { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Alt text for the image, or accessible label for a monogram / icon avatar.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Alt { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Text monogram (e.g. "JS") when there is no image.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Initials { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Material Icons ligature name, as a fallback identity glyph.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Icon { get; set; }

    /// <summary>sm = 28 · md = 40 (default) · lg = 56.</summary>
    [Parameter] public OdsSize Size { get; set; } = OdsSize.Md;

    /// <summary>neutral (default) or tide (brand-tinted).</summary>
    [Parameter] public OdsAvatarTone Tone { get; set; } = OdsAvatarTone.Neutral;

    /// <summary>Rounded-rect (8px) instead of a circle — for account / file / record tiles.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Square { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// How an image meets the frame. Cover (default) square-crops — a photograph. Contain letterboxes
    /// it on a neutral ground with a 3:1 boundary — a logo, which carries transparency and must never
    /// be cut. Ignored when there is no <see cref="Src"/>.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public OdsAvatarFit Fit { get; set; } = OdsAvatarFit.Cover;

    /// <summary>
    /// Fires when the image fails to load. Swap to the identity glyph here; the failure is never
    /// surfaced to the user.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnError { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Custom background tint (any CSS color) — the DS Avatar's <c>{ bg, fg }</c> tone, used for
    /// per-category record avatars (e.g. contact type). Overrides <see cref="Tone"/> when set.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Bg { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Custom foreground/icon color paired with <see cref="Bg"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Fg { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public Dictionary<string, object>? UserAttributes { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Icon/monogram avatar with no accessible name — decorative, hidden from AT.</summary>
    private bool IsDecorative => string.IsNullOrEmpty(Src) && string.IsNullOrEmpty(Alt);

    /// <summary>Meaningful `img` only for a labelled, non-image avatar.</summary>
    private string? AvatarRole => string.IsNullOrEmpty(Src) && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Alt) ? "img" : null;

    /// <summary>The contain ground is only a ground when there is actually an image to letterbox.</summary>
    private bool IsContained => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Src) && Fit == OdsAvatarFit.Contain;

    private string RootClass =>
        string.Join(' ', new[]
        {
            "odc-avatar",
            Square ? "sq" : null,
            IsContained ? "contain" : null,
            Class,
        }.Where(part => !string.IsNullOrEmpty(part)));

    private string SizeStyle => Size switch
    {
        OdsSize.Sm => "width:28px;height:28px;font-size:0.75rem;",
        OdsSize.Lg => "width:56px;height:56px;font-size:1.25rem;",
        _ => "width:40px;height:40px;font-size:0.9375rem;",
    };

    // A custom { bg, fg } tone (DS Avatar) overrides the named MudAvatar color via inline style. The
    // contain ground is its own background, so a caller-supplied Bg is not applied over it.
    private string AvatarStyle => string.IsNullOrEmpty(Bg) && string.IsNullOrEmpty(Fg)
        ? SizeStyle
        : $"{SizeStyle}{(string.IsNullOrEmpty(Bg) || IsContained ? "" : $"background:{Bg};")}{(string.IsNullOrEmpty(Fg) ? "" : $"color:{Fg};")}";

    private Task OnErrorAsync() => OnError.InvokeAsync();
}
